        "message": "Affected versions of io.netty:netty-codec-http are vulnerable to Inconsistent Interpretation of HTTP Requests ('HTTP Request/Response Smuggling'). Netty's HTTP chunked‐encoding parser treats a lone LF in a chunk extension as the end of the size line (instead of requiring CRLF per RFC 9112). If a front‐end proxy instead treats that LF as part of the extension, an attacker can craft a \"funky chunks\" payload that the proxy sees as one request but Netty splits into two, enabling standard HTTP request‐smuggling attacks—bypassing access controls and corrupting responses to other clients.",
        "metadata": {
          "confidence": "HIGH",
